When Is Heavy Flow a Concern?

If you regularly need to change your pad extremely frequently because it becomes saturated very quickly, it may be worth discussing your menstrual flow with a healthcare professional.

This is especially important if heavy bleeding is accompanied by dizziness, weakness, unusual tiredness, severe pain, or repeated leakage.

Simple Period Hygiene Matters

Changing your sanitary pad regularly does not need to be complicated. Check your pad throughout the day, choose the right absorbency, maintain hand hygiene, and replace the product whenever it becomes uncomfortable or saturated.

Understanding your own menstrual flow is the best way to develop a practical pad-changing routine.
